{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed: Gerrit change 2139 (commit 5d9ddc14389). Shape: period=300, evaluation_periods=5, datapoints_to_alarm=3, threshold=0 Sum>0, notBreaching — isolated transient (<=2 breaching periods incl. boundary straddle) never pages; sustained stream pages at ~15 min (3rd breaching period), 3-of-5 tolerating up to 2 phase-gap periods per the plan-review finding on N-of-N fragility. Alarm description heredoc updated with rationale + this ticket id. Validation: terraform fmt -check PASS, terraform validate PASS (1.10.5 = CI version), make lint + typecheck + complexity ratchet green. APPLICATION PATH (AC 4): landing via Gerrit does NOT apply to AWS — applies are MANUAL per infra/runbooks/provision-restore.md §plan-before-apply (terraform plan -out plan.tfplan → review → terraform apply plan.tfplan). The daily terraform-drift sweep (.github/workflows/terraform-drift.yml, cron 17:06 UTC) will FAIL on the non-empty plan until an operator applies — that is the designed committed-but-unapplied signal. I am not running terraform apply myself per the ticket instruction."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787448516247693001,"uuid":"d2483a0f-03c2-4bc1-99eb-250a2a16d5c2"}